---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { chapters } from '../data/chapters';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const parts = [
  { title: 'I · Engineering in the Age of AI', message: 'Why engineering is changing — and how to plan under uncertainty.', future: 'The New Engineering Paradigm · Planning Under Uncertainty' },
  { title: 'II · Building Engineering Knowledge', message: 'Connect engineering information, test assumptions, and specify progressively.', future: 'Engineering Knowledge as Code · Learning Through Models · Spec-Driven Development' },
  { title: 'III · Engineering with AI Agents', message: 'Direct bounded agent work and integrate small, reviewable increments.', future: 'Directing Agents · Reviewable Increments · Continuous Integration' },
  { title: 'IV · Trust, Decisions and Evolution', message: 'Interpret evidence, govern change, and keep engineering knowledge coherent.', future: 'Verification & Evidence · Authority · Scale · Integrated Environment' },
];
---
<Layout title="Engineering at the Speed of AI">
  <p class="eyebrow">Executable Engineering Lab · A practical learning environment</p>
  <h1>Engineering at the Speed of AI.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Digital Engineering connects knowledge across disciplines. AI agents can accelerate exploration and implementation. The challenge is to use both without losing control of engineering decisions, architecture, or evidence.</p>
  <p>Follow a fictional Distributed Monitoring System from uncertain intent toward progressively more informed engineering decisions. Explore how software, electronics, mechanical design, integration and verification contribute at different speeds.</p>
  <p><strong>Our approach:</strong> specify what we know, explore what we don't, verify what we build, and preserve what we learn.</p>
  <p><a href={`${base}learn/`}>Explore the learning path →</a> · <a href={`${base}lab/`}>Open the existing coverage lab</a></p>
  <h2>Four connected questions</h2>
  <div class="parts">
    {parts.map(part => <section class="card"><h3>{part.title}</h3><p>{part.message}</p><p class="future"><strong>V2 direction:</strong> {part.future}</p></section>)}
  </div>
  <h2>Explore the published lessons</h2>
  <p>The original twelve lessons remain available while the new curriculum is developed. They focus on a deliberately limited single-sensor teaching model. The new multidisciplinary demonstrations and recorded agent workflows are <strong>planned, not yet implemented</strong>.</p>
  <section class="cards" aria-label="Published lessons">
    {chapters.map((chapter, index) => <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Existing lesson {String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</p><h3><a href={`${base}learn/${chapter.path}/`}>{chapter.title}</a></h3><p>{chapter.summary}</p></article>)}
  </section>
  <p><a href={`${base}reference/`}>Inspect engineering sources</a> · <a href="https://github.com/And-Gu/executable-engineering-lab">See the repository</a></p>
</Layout>
<style>
  .parts {display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,15rem),1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.5rem 0 3rem}
  .parts .card {background:var(--surface)}
  .parts h3 {margin-top:0}
  .future {font-size:.88rem}
</style>
